{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-76189" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}5y{e}^{-x}\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the section of the curve $y={e}^{x}$ for $\\,0\\le x\\le e?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/state.json" "file_sha256" "83696588766f5f9c53de2edda6efd15c92466a73316a4a838046181fc899a248"} {"question" "q-76189" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the given curve is of the form $y=y(x).$ Therefore, by setting $x=t,$ we have $y=y(t)={e}^{t}.$ This gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨t,{e}^{t}⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le e\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})j \\\\  & =i+{e}^{t}\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+({e}^{t})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{e}^{2t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=5y{e}^{-x}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =5{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{-t}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{e}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{e}5\\cdot \\sqrt{1+{e}^{2t}}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{e}\\sqrt{1+{e}^{2t}}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/state.json" "file_sha256" "83696588766f5f9c53de2edda6efd15c92466a73316a4a838046181fc899a248"} {"question" "q-76189" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1482712abb5c208c992ec4925bf68af0f16d1fdd80ad065ea77a95a82133c534"} {"question" "q-76189" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/state.json" "file_sha256" "83696588766f5f9c53de2edda6efd15c92466a73316a4a838046181fc899a248"} {"question" "q-76189" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5{\\int }_{0}^{e}\\sqrt{1+{e}^{2t}}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "5{\\int }_{0}^{e}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{1+{e}^{2t}}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "5{\\int }_{0}^{e}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{t+{e}^{t}}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{e}t{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{e}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{1+{e}^{2t}}\\,\\text{d}t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/state.json" "file_sha256" "83696588766f5f9c53de2edda6efd15c92466a73316a4a838046181fc899a248"} {"question" "q-76189" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5{\\int }_{0}^{e}\\sqrt{1+{e}^{2t}}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/state.json" "file_sha256" "83696588766f5f9c53de2edda6efd15c92466a73316a4a838046181fc899a248"} {"question" "q-76415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the section of the curve $y=2{x}^{2}$ between the points $(1,2)$ and $(3,18)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/state.json" "file_sha256" "83696588766f5f9c53de2edda6efd15c92466a73316a4a838046181fc899a248"} {"question" "q-76415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the given curve is of the form $y=y(x).$ Therefore, by setting $x=t,$ we have $y=y(t)=2{t}^{2}.$ This gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨t,2{t}^{2}⟩,\\,1\\le t\\le 3\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2})j \\\\  & =i+4t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(4t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+16{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}2{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot \\sqrt{1+16{t}^{2}}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{1}^{3}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\sqrt{1+16{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/state.json" "file_sha256" "83696588766f5f9c53de2edda6efd15c92466a73316a4a838046181fc899a248"} {"question" "q-76415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1482712abb5c208c992ec4925bf68af0f16d1fdd80ad065ea77a95a82133c534"} {"question" "q-76415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/state.json" "file_sha256" "83696588766f5f9c53de2edda6efd15c92466a73316a4a838046181fc899a248"} {"question" "q-76415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\sqrt{1+16{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "2{\\int }_{1}^{3}{t}^{2}\\,\\sqrt{1+16{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "2{\\int }_{1}^{3}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\sqrt{1+16{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "8{\\int }_{1}^{3}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{2}\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{16}+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{3}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/state.json" "file_sha256" "83696588766f5f9c53de2edda6efd15c92466a73316a4a838046181fc899a248"} {"question" "q-76415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{\\int }_{1}^{3}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\sqrt{1+16{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/state.json" "file_sha256" "83696588766f5f9c53de2edda6efd15c92466a73316a4a838046181fc899a248"} {"question" "q-76480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{C}\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is given by $y=\\frac{1}{x},$ $\\,1\\le x\\le \\sqrt[4]{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/state.json" "file_sha256" "83696588766f5f9c53de2edda6efd15c92466a73316a4a838046181fc899a248"} {"question" "q-76480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the given curve is of the form $y=y(x).$ Therefore, by setting $x=t,$ we have $y=y(t)=\\frac{1}{t}.$ This gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨t,\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩,\\,1\\le t\\le \\sqrt[4]{2}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})j \\\\  & =i-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{(-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{{x}^{3}}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{4{(\\frac{1}{t})}^{2}}{{t}^{3}}=\\frac{4}{{t}^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}3{x}^{5}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt[4]{2}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt[4]{2}}\\frac{4}{{t}^{5}}\\cdot \\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt[4]{2}}\\frac{1}{{t}^{5}}\\,\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=1+\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}$, $\\text{d}u=-\\frac{4}{{t}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt[4]{2}}\\frac{1}{{t}^{5}}\\,\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}}\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{2}^{3/2}{u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}{|}_{2}^{3/2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}(\\sqrt{{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{3}}-\\sqrt{{2}^{3}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}(\\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{4}-2\\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(8\\sqrt{2}-3\\sqrt{6})\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/state.json" "file_sha256" "83696588766f5f9c53de2edda6efd15c92466a73316a4a838046181fc899a248"} {"question" "q-76480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1482712abb5c208c992ec4925bf68af0f16d1fdd80ad065ea77a95a82133c534"} {"question" "q-76480" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/state.json" "file_sha256" "83696588766f5f9c53de2edda6efd15c92466a73316a4a838046181fc899a248"} {"question" "q-76480" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12\\sqrt{6}"] ["math" "16\\sqrt{2}-6\\sqrt{6}"] ["math" "2(16\\sqrt{2}-6\\sqrt{6})"] ["math" "32\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}(8\\sqrt{2}-3\\sqrt{6})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/state.json" "file_sha256" "83696588766f5f9c53de2edda6efd15c92466a73316a4a838046181fc899a248"} {"question" "q-76480" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{6}(8\\sqrt{2}-3\\sqrt{6})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/state.json" "file_sha256" "83696588766f5f9c53de2edda6efd15c92466a73316a4a838046181fc899a248"} {"question" "q-148199" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}({x}^{3}-2y)\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the section of the curve $y=2-\\frac{x}{2}$ for $\\,0\\le x\\le 2?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/state.json" "file_sha256" "83696588766f5f9c53de2edda6efd15c92466a73316a4a838046181fc899a248"} {"question" "q-148199" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the given curve is of the form $y=y(x).$ Therefore, by setting $x=t,$ we have $y=y(t)=2-\\frac{t}{2}.$ This gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨t,2-\\frac{t}{2}⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le 2\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2-\\frac{t}{2})j \\\\  & =i-\\frac{1}{2}\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)={x}^{3}-2y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & ={t}^{3}-2(2-\\frac{t}{2})={t}^{3}+t-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({t}^{3}+t-4)\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({t}^{3}+t-4)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/state.json" "file_sha256" "83696588766f5f9c53de2edda6efd15c92466a73316a4a838046181fc899a248"} {"question" "q-148199" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1482712abb5c208c992ec4925bf68af0f16d1fdd80ad065ea77a95a82133c534"} {"question" "q-148199" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/state.json" "file_sha256" "83696588766f5f9c53de2edda6efd15c92466a73316a4a838046181fc899a248"} {"question" "q-148199" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({t}^{3}+2t-8)\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({t}^{3}-t-4)\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(2{t}^{3}+t-8)\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(t-4)\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({t}^{3}+t-4)\\,\\text{d}t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/state.json" "file_sha256" "83696588766f5f9c53de2edda6efd15c92466a73316a4a838046181fc899a248"} {"question" "q-148199" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({t}^{3}+t-4)\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/state.json" "file_sha256" "83696588766f5f9c53de2edda6efd15c92466a73316a4a838046181fc899a248"} {"question" "q-148216" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral of the function $f(x,y)=x+y$ along the line $y=x,$ $\\,0\\le x\\le 3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/state.json" "file_sha256" "83696588766f5f9c53de2edda6efd15c92466a73316a4a838046181fc899a248"} {"question" "q-148216" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the given curve is of the form $y=y(x).$ Therefore, by setting $x=t,$ we have $y=y(t)=t.$ This gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨t,\\,t⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le 3\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =i+\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=x+y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =t+t=2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2t\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\,{t}^{2}{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}({3}^{2}-{0}^{2}) \\\\  & =9\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/state.json" "file_sha256" "83696588766f5f9c53de2edda6efd15c92466a73316a4a838046181fc899a248"} {"question" "q-148216" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1482712abb5c208c992ec4925bf68af0f16d1fdd80ad065ea77a95a82133c534"} {"question" "q-148216" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066999/state.json" "file_sha256" "83696588766f5f9c53de2edda6efd15c92466a73316a4a838046181fc899a248"} {